WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:08.340
My dearest dolly,

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:10.580
Because I am writing in my bed

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:12.960
This won't be so terribly neat

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:16.080
But nevermind I'll just go on scrawling

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:18.720
For Dolly is interested in it all the same.

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:32.780
Hello and welcome back to another video. If you thought me going through Einsteins grades was an invasion of his privacy

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:36.920
Well, the worst was yet to come. Today, as was highly requested

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:40.240
I'm going to be going through Einsteins love letters.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:44.120
Now, the originals are all referenced in the description.

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:48.320
These ones I printed out myself onto some tea stained paper and

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:50.360
Well, they're pretty spicy.

00:00:50.519 --> 00:00:54.619
They show that Einstein struggled with some of the same problems in

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:59.980
relationships and love that many people do and they also show that at times

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:02.620
Einstein's mind was lost in space,

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:08.960
thinking about physics, but at other times his mind was lost in love. So let's have a look at them

00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:15.320
Einstein met his first wife Mileva while they were both students at university

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:18.280
But that is not where this story starts.

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:25.460
No, we are starting with Einstein's high-school romance, a girl called Marie Winteler

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:27.479
Beloved sweetheart!

00:01:27.479 --> 00:01:33.499
Many, many thanks sweetheart for your charming little letter, which made me endlessly happy.

00:01:33.719 --> 00:01:38.659
It is so wonderful to be able to press to one's heart such a bit of paper

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:46.240
which two so dear little eyes have lovingly beheld... only now do I realize how indispensable

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:49.680
My dear little sunshine has become to my happiness

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:52.540
My mother has also taken you to her heart

00:01:52.859 --> 00:01:59.599
Even though she does not know you. We can see that Einsteins mother did approve of this little relationship

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:05.990
Because she signed the bottom of this letter herself. 'Without having read the letter I send you

00:02:06.299 --> 00:02:09.199
cordial greetings! From Pauline Einstein.'

00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:14.820
This approval becomes relevant later on when things turn a little sour

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:18.400
and the families no longer like each other that much.

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:24.380
This girl Marie is someone who Einstein met while he was studying at

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:27.509
the Aarau school in Switzerland

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:32.850
Einstein actually lodged with Marie's family as her father was a

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:40.589
professor at the school, and this letter was written while Einstein was back in his own hometown for the holidays.

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:43.559
Here's a reply from Marie:

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:49.709
'Beloved sweetheart! Your little basket arrived today and in vain did I strain my eyes

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:57.570
looking for a little note, even though the mere sight of your dear handwriting in the address was enough to make me happy.'

00:02:58.140 --> 00:03:05.160
It finishes off with, 'all I can say is that I love you for all eternity sweetheart,

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:07.940
and may god preserve and protect you.'

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:09.600
A spoiler,

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:13.360
eternity didn't last for quite as long as they thought

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:18.540
fast forward about a year and we have a letter written from Einstein to

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:22.290
Pauline Winteler and that is Marie's mother

00:03:22.570 --> 00:03:29.009
It's addressed dear mommy, which is a little confusing some Einsteins mother's name is also Pauline

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:34.530
but this is him writing to his girlfriend's mother and it's not the nicest of letters.

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:37.919
In fact, it's almost a bit of a breakup note

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:45.179
'I am writing you so soon in order to cut short an inner struggle whose outcome is, in fact,

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:48.180
already firmly settled in my mind.

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:52.560
I cannot come to visit you at Whitsuntide.

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:57.300
This must have been some invitation for Einstein to join the family somewhere.

00:03:57.430 --> 00:04:00.780
He speaks about pain, which he has brought her child,

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:07.060
pain that was brought through his thoughtlessness and ignorance of her delicate nature

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:13.380
So this sounds like they've freshly broken up and Einstein is cutting ties with the family.

00:04:13.780 --> 00:04:20.190
There's an interesting sentence here as he goes on to describe what he's up to and he says that, 'Strenuous

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:23.310
intellectual work and looking at God's Nature

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:31.570
are there reconciling fortifying, yet relentlessly strict angels that shall lead me through all of life's troubles.'

00:04:32.420 --> 00:04:36.680
This letter was May 1897

00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:40.200
and by February 1898

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:45.320
we have the first letter that I'll show here addressed to Mileva Maric.

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:50.619
Mileva was a classmate of Einstein's at ETH.

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:56.470
She was the only female there studying physics and at the time of this letter she was actually

00:04:56.810 --> 00:05:02.110
Away from Zurich and she was in Heidelberg pursuing some of her studies there.

00:05:02.540 --> 00:05:09.670
Einstein says that he is very happy about her intention to continue her studies here again, and he's referring to

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:17.770
ETH. He also goes on to tell her about some of the material they've covered and he mentions the infamous Weber

00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:20.540
Who lectured on heat.

00:05:20.540 --> 00:05:23.380
Now, if you've seen my video on Einstein's grades

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:30.159
You will know that Weber is a little notorious, they didn't end their relationship on good terms.

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:33.300
It's now 1899,

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:39.620
we have another letter here to Mileva. This is one that highlights the fact that they used to study together a lot.

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:41.180
He says,

00:05:41.180 --> 00:05:43.810
'When I was reading Helmholtz for the first time,

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:49.689
it seemed inconceivable that you were not here with me and now it's not much better.'

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:54.730
So it seems that Einstein really does enjoy her company. On the other hand

00:05:54.730 --> 00:06:00.129
he makes a note here about his family who he kind of finds a bit narrow-minded.

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:03.130
He's struggling to relate with them anymore.

00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:09.520
'It is strange how a way of life will eventually change us and all the nuances of our soul

00:06:09.980 --> 00:06:16.300
deep inside we become so incomprehensible to each other that we are unable to actively

00:06:16.580 --> 00:06:19.780
empathize with the other and feel what moves the other.'

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:28.100
Albert finds in Mileva something that he can't find in his family, which is sort of an intellectual equal

00:06:28.100 --> 00:06:34.760
Someone who he can discuss Helmholtz with. Perhaps that is why Albert is so attracted to her.

00:06:34.970 --> 00:06:39.220
She is a couple of years older than him and probably quite mature

00:06:39.800 --> 00:06:44.780
Probably a lot more so than Albert found in his first relationship with Marie.

00:06:45.540 --> 00:06:52.249
Here's another letter from Mileva. She says, 'All this time I have not gotten further than our garden

00:06:52.410 --> 00:06:58.459
We now don't go to town at all. There have been many cases of scarlet fever and

00:06:59.250 --> 00:07:03.829
diphtheria, so that we prefer staying in our own fresh and healthy air.'

00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:09.679
So it shows that lock down vibes are nothing new. At the bottom of this video

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:13.880
You can see some of the nicknames that these two used referring to each other.

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:19.969
This one is signed off your Doxerl, which is the name for 'dolly'.

00:07:20.310 --> 00:07:26.630
Here's another letter from Einstein and in it he tells Mileva that her letters always make him

00:07:26.630 --> 00:07:30.200
So happy that everybody teases him for it.

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:38.880
He also goes on to mention that his sister is following in his footsteps by moving to Aarau to

00:07:38.940 --> 00:07:41.780
complete her high school education

00:07:41.780 --> 00:07:43.820
He takes it upon himself to

00:07:43.820 --> 00:07:49.540
mention the little daughter there who he fell so terribly in love with four years ago.

00:07:49.540 --> 00:07:51.980
And here he is referring to Marie

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:56.600
I'm not quite sure why he says this but he then says,

00:07:56.820 --> 00:08:02.260
'if I saw the girl again a few times, I would surely get crazy again.

00:08:02.270 --> 00:08:05.600
I am aware of that and fear it like fire.'

00:08:06.180 --> 00:08:08.840
Maybe something got lost in translation,

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:12.920
but it seems like Einstein is telling his current love interest

00:08:12.920 --> 00:08:17.320
that he's at risk of falling back in love with his ex.

00:08:18.780 --> 00:08:25.980
Here's a short and sweet note from Mileva addressed to one of her pet names for Albert, 'Johonsl'

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:27.260
and she says,

00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:32.539
'Since I like you so much and you are so far away that I cannot give you a kiss,

00:08:32.570 --> 00:08:39.020
I am now writing this little letter and am asking you whether you like me as much as I do you?

00:08:39.659 --> 00:08:41.659
Answer me immediately.

00:08:41.840 --> 00:08:48.420
Thousand kisses from your Doxerl. Albert and Mileva's marriage did end in divorce,

00:08:48.420 --> 00:08:52.240
but these letters show us that in the in-between years

00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:58.000
and at the start of their relationship there was very much a lot of affection between the two

00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:01.780
We then have the poem to Mileva which was written in bed

00:09:01.780 --> 00:09:05.840
and under it some more disapproval from Einstein's mum.

00:09:05.840 --> 00:09:10.320
'I go into Mama's room. First I have to tell her about the examination

00:09:10.840 --> 00:09:15.380
Then she asked me innocently: "So, what will become of Dolly?"

00:09:15.380 --> 00:09:17.300
"My wife," say I,

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:23.220
equally innocently, but prepared for a real scene. This then ensued immediately.

00:09:23.570 --> 00:09:28.629
Mama, threw herself on the bed buried her head in the pillow and cried like a child.

00:09:29.600 --> 00:09:31.990
After she had recovered from the initial shock,

00:09:32.029 --> 00:09:38.979
She immediately switched to a desperate offensive. "You are ruining your future and blocking your path through life.

00:09:39.620 --> 00:09:42.909
That woman cannot gain entrance to a decent family."

00:09:42.940 --> 00:09:48.609
It seemed that Einstein's mum disapproved of this relationship because she thought that

00:09:49.010 --> 00:09:54.669
Einstein was too young to marry and settle down. He was about 21 at the time.

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:59.120
She thought he was throwing away his career prospects

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:06.060
She also didn't consider Mileva to be very beautiful. At this time where a woman could be either

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:08.269
beautiful or smart,

00:10:08.269 --> 00:10:12.638
Einstein's mum makes remarks about Mileva being a smart one.

00:10:12.860 --> 00:10:19.479
But as we know, Albert was a very independent person and three years after this letter

00:10:19.880 --> 00:10:24.729
Albert and Mileva did go on to get married and they had some children together.

00:10:24.949 --> 00:10:30.789
He also mentions how he feels restless without Mileva in his presence. He says,

00:10:31.339 --> 00:10:38.499
'When I do not have you I feel as if I were not whole. When I am sitting, I would like to walk;

00:10:38.740 --> 00:10:42.160
when I am walking, I look forward to being at home,

00:10:42.340 --> 00:10:45.680
when I amuse myself, I would like to study,

00:10:45.680 --> 00:10:50.900
and when I am studying I feel a lack of contemplativeness and repose.

00:10:50.900 --> 00:10:55.180
When I go to bed, I am not satisfied with how I passed the day.'

00:10:55.180 --> 00:11:03.480
I like this passage here because it really shows the human aspect of Einstein and the fact that

00:11:03.500 --> 00:11:10.960
Yes, his mind was on all things physics and thinking of some of the biggest ideas

00:11:10.960 --> 00:11:18.480
there are, but his mind was also in love and he's feeling lovesick and he can't focus

00:11:18.600 --> 00:11:23.320
And that's, you know, a side of Einstein that you never hear about

00:11:23.320 --> 00:11:31.520
Now, if you remember back to the first letter, we had Einstein's mum Pauline giving a glowing review to his first girlfriend

00:11:31.520 --> 00:11:33.320
Marie Winteler

00:11:33.320 --> 00:11:35.799
Although that is long in the past now

00:11:35.800 --> 00:11:36.490
and in fact

00:11:36.490 --> 00:11:40.930
This is a very nasty note written from Pauline Einstein

00:11:41.210 --> 00:11:44.739
to Pauline Winteler when talking about Marie

00:11:44.810 --> 00:11:48.369
She says, 'that we don't want anything to do with her,

00:11:48.370 --> 00:11:51.729
there is constant friction with Albert because of it.'

00:11:51.920 --> 00:11:58.930
Now, these families are still linked together because I believe Einstein's younger sister Maja

00:11:59.450 --> 00:12:03.460
Went to our Aarau and also boarded with the family.

00:12:03.640 --> 00:12:11.289
In fact, Maja goes on to marry Marie's brother Paul and becomes Maja Winteler.

00:12:11.600 --> 00:12:17.320
Although in this letter Einstein's mum says that, 'we should not talk anywhere about an engagement.

00:12:17.990 --> 00:12:22.240
This Miss Marie is causing me the bitterest hours of my life,

00:12:22.580 --> 00:12:28.920
if it were in my power, I would make every possible effort to banish her from our horizon,

00:12:29.240 --> 00:12:31.580
I really dislike her.

00:12:31.580 --> 00:12:35.710
But I have lost every influence on Albert. You can imagine,

00:12:36.320 --> 00:12:41.320
dear Frau Professor, how unhappy this makes me. Pauline Einstein'

00:12:41.870 --> 00:12:47.500
Not sure totally what is going on here whether Albert is still seeing Marie in some way,

00:12:47.840 --> 00:12:54.540
but definitely these families are no longer on good terms, although they are forever linked

00:12:54.640 --> 00:12:57.200
thanks to Maja and Paul.

00:12:57.200 --> 00:13:03.340
While we're on the topic of hate, let's fast forward a few years to 1912.

00:13:03.340 --> 00:13:10.220
This is after Einstein's miracle year of productivity which was in 1905.

00:13:10.220 --> 00:13:12.360
and here we have a letter to

00:13:12.920 --> 00:13:17.820
Elsa Lowenthal, who was actually Einstein's cousin.

00:13:17.920 --> 00:13:21.140
Now yes, Einstein does go on to marry Elsa,

00:13:21.140 --> 00:13:25.000
she becomes his second wife after he divorces Mileva

00:13:25.240 --> 00:13:32.600
but him and Mileva are still together when this letter was written, they didn't divorce until 1919.

00:13:32.900 --> 00:13:40.920
Einstein says to Elsa that, 'I can't even begin to tell you how fond I have become of you during these days.'

00:13:41.510 --> 00:13:47.110
He also that mentions that he had some kind of fleeting crush on Elsa's sister, Paula,

00:13:47.320 --> 00:13:50.240
but he assures her that is over now

00:13:50.240 --> 00:13:57.720
He says, 'When I think of the bad relationship between my wife and Maja (his sister) or my mother,

00:13:58.160 --> 00:14:03.219
then I must admit to myself, sadly, that I find all three of them quite

00:14:03.740 --> 00:14:10.810
unlikable! But I have to have someone to love, otherwise life is miserable. And this someone is you;

00:14:11.390 --> 00:14:15.550
you cannot do anything about it, since I'm not asking you for permission.

00:14:15.860 --> 00:14:19.809
I am the absolute ruler in the netherworld of my

00:14:20.380 --> 00:14:24.440
imagination, or at least that is what I choose to think.'

00:14:24.440 --> 00:14:29.440
Now, I don't find that sentence too romantic, but it must have worked out for him

00:14:30.080 --> 00:14:32.660
'Kisses from your Albert.'

00:14:32.660 --> 00:14:35.980
This letter ends with a spicy P.S.

00:14:36.100 --> 00:14:40.300
which is him saying, 'If this is what you want, then write me again.

00:14:40.300 --> 00:14:44.649
I will always destroy the letters as you have requested

00:14:44.890 --> 00:14:47.680
I have already destroyed the first one.'

00:14:47.900 --> 00:14:53.110
So I think they knew that this relationship of theirs was not going to be well received

00:14:53.740 --> 00:14:57.100
and that they were in their best interest to keep it secret.

00:14:57.860 --> 00:15:03.699
'Dearest Else, I am writing so late because I have misgivings about our affair.

00:15:03.700 --> 00:15:07.480
I have the feeling that it will not be good for the two of us as

00:15:07.640 --> 00:15:11.199
well as for the others if we form a closer attachment.

00:15:11.570 --> 00:15:15.249
So, I am writing to you today for the last time.'

00:15:15.650 --> 00:15:20.739
This breakup letter of sorts with Else while he's still married to Mileva

00:15:21.170 --> 00:15:25.300
shows how heartbroken Einstein is to be cutting off this relationship.

00:15:25.880 --> 00:15:29.860
But never fear, next year in 1913,

00:15:29.860 --> 00:15:36.440
things are back on Einstein says, 'Now we will be together and will rejoice in each other. Unfortunately,

00:15:37.180 --> 00:15:44.860
this won't happen until the end of the winter semester, because I could not bring myself to break off things here so rapidly.

00:15:44.980 --> 00:15:47.680
Give my regards to Uncle and Aunt.'

00:15:48.260 --> 00:15:53.280
Here, he must be referring to his uncle and aunt which is Elsa's parents.

00:15:53.480 --> 00:15:59.900
Certainly a taboo relationship now, and I'm not sure to what extent it was then.

00:15:59.900 --> 00:16:02.540
This next letter from 1914

00:16:02.540 --> 00:16:10.240
showed some of the friction that the relationship faced. 'Dear Elsa, didn't I tell you that all hell would break loose?'

00:16:10.240 --> 00:16:15.720
He refers to Mileva as Miza and says that, 'she is by nature

00:16:15.720 --> 00:16:22.780
unfriendly and mistrustful.' He says, 'You showed her kindness. But she obviously distrusts you.'

00:16:22.780 --> 00:16:29.480
Now, that doesn't seem surprising to me seeing as this Elsa character is about to steal her husband away.

00:16:29.690 --> 00:16:31.960
This next letter, I really wanted to show you.

00:16:32.180 --> 00:16:39.039
It's written a month later to Elsa and Einstein is apologizing for being a poor letter writer.

00:16:39.200 --> 00:16:45.849
He says, 'I cannot find the time to write because I am occupied with truly great things.

00:16:46.240 --> 00:16:51.440
Day and night I rack my brain in an effort to penetrate more deeply

00:16:51.440 --> 00:16:57.220
into the things that I gradually discovered in the past two years and that represent an

00:16:57.700 --> 00:17:02.100
unprecedented advance in the fundamental problem of physics.'

00:17:02.300 --> 00:17:07.660
I think this is a nice insight into Einstein's opinions of his own work.

00:17:07.900 --> 00:17:11.660
He says that he must now write a long article,

00:17:11.660 --> 00:17:16.660
since his most distinguished colleagues refuse to accept his point of view

00:17:16.840 --> 00:17:22.260
Einstein did have to put in a lot of effort to convince other physicists of his work.

00:17:22.360 --> 00:17:25.980
And I think this is a fitting final letter to show.

00:17:25.980 --> 00:17:30.800
It again reminds us that Einstein's life is interwoven with

00:17:30.800 --> 00:17:33.600
love, life and physics.

00:17:33.600 --> 00:17:38.600
You can't really separate his correspondence with any of these girls

00:17:38.600 --> 00:17:44.360
and his obsession with working on figuring out some of these fundamental ideas.

00:17:44.360 --> 00:17:46.940
At his most excited times,

00:17:46.940 --> 00:17:52.180
he is talking to these girls about his findings or discussing his studies.

00:17:52.180 --> 00:17:59.420
I hope you have enjoyed this little insight into an aspect of Einstein's life that you don't often see.

